                                   "title":  "Letterboxd review of 35 Shots of Rum",
                                   "snippet":  "[Letterboxd Review of \"35 Shots of Rum\"] I want to call this--and pretty much any Claire Denis film--a \"rumination,\" but that implies that the goal is something rational, something of the mind, rather than an emotional understanding. Perhaps it\u0027s more fair to qualify her work as \"emotional ruminations,\" and here, the loose, poetic lens of her cameras has captured many small snippets of an unlikely family\u0027s life in the midst of flux. This implies a lot more action that is seen, but all the same, there is an undercurrent of chaos to it, glimpses of turmoil, unspoken conflicts. The film uses this to linger on many threads, many ideas, w",
                                   "link":  "https://letterboxd.com/film/35-shots-of-rum/"
                               },
                               {
                                   "title":  "Letterboxd review of 35 Shots of Rum",
                                   "snippet":  "[Letterboxd Review of \"35 Shots of Rum\"] \"I didn\u0027t think I\u0027d miss it.\"claire denis is either using really dark sorcery and sacrificing infant children to be this superlative in dealing with the camera and its subjects, to extract the deepest possible emotional reaction with so much as a twinge musical note, someones dark eyes looking at someone they love, pitter patter of train tracks, or she really is that fucking good. idiots will probably go with the former.",
